Content:
@RonFilipkowski Starbucks in NYC had for-hire signs up on the door ($25/hr), while 20-30 customers waiting in line. 
 Such attractive hourly wage nobody wants it. It shows how little Americans are willing to work, and how much they want in return. 
 Low-end production can’t make it back to USA.

Translated:
